 "poem": "The sky is on her; she glides along,\nShe leads a swan in the water's sea;\nAnd he has his bonnet and helmet\nOn her shoulder, hairless she.\nHe says to me: \"This morning\nI came with her and I brought away\nA parrot and a feather,\nUpon which now today\nWe play until at nightfall again\nTwo birds have devoured away\nAll our treasures.\" Again\nHe has his helmet, gray",
